<script is:inline>
  const questions = [
    {
      q: "In 'A Letter to God', why did Lencho describe the raindrops falling from the sky as 'new coins'?",
      opts: [
        "Because he was hallucinating due to starvation",
        "Because good rainfall promised a prosperous corn harvest that would yield money",
        "Because the raindrops were actually carrying silver coins in them",
        "Because the postmaster had sent money in the form of raindrops"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Lencho compared the big drops to ten-cent pieces and small drops to fives because rain was essential for his cornfield to prosper, which would translate into money for his family."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the extreme irony at the end of 'A Letter to God'?",
      opts: [
        "The hail stopped right when the crop was destroyed",
        "The post office employees who charitably gave money were branded 'a bunch of crooks' by Lencho",
        "God sent more money than Lencho had requested",
        "Lencho became rich overnight without the harvest"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "The postmaster and his staff sacrificed their own earnings out of pure kindness, yet Lencho suspected they had stolen the missing 30 pesos."
    },
    {
      q: "According to Nelson Mandela, what is the profound relationship between the oppressor and the oppressed?",
      opts: [
        "The oppressor is superior because of military dominance",
        "Both the oppressor and the oppressed are robbed of their humanity",
        "The oppressed must wage a war of revenge to eliminate the oppressor",
        "Freedom is only required by the oppressed, not the oppressor"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Mandela observed that a man who takes away another man's freedom is a prisoner of hatred; thus both oppressor and oppressed lack true freedom."
    },
    {
      q: "What are the 'twin obligations' described by Nelson Mandela in his autobiography?",
      opts: [
        "Obligation to physical health and spiritual salvation",
        "Obligation to one's family/parents and obligation to one's people/country",
        "Obligation to the white minority and the African National Congress",
        "Obligation to earn wealth and obligation to obey the law"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Mandela states every man has twin obligations: first to his family, parents, wife, and children; second to his people, community, and country."
    },
    {
      q: "What compelled the young seagull to finally take his first flight in Liam O'Flaherty's story?",
      opts: [
        "A fierce gust of wind that blew him off the ledge",
        "His intense hunger when his mother brought fish close to his beak and halted",
        "The threat of being killed by his father",
        "A predator bird attacking his nest"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Maddened by 24 hours of hunger, the young seagull dived at the fish his mother dangled, plunging into space where his wings instinctively spread."
    },
    {
      q: "In 'The Black Aeroplane', what did the woman in the Paris Control Tower confirm to the narrator upon his landing?",
      opts: [
        "That the mysterious pilot was an undercover military officer",
        "That no other aeroplanes were flying in the storm that night besides his own",
        "That the black aeroplane had run out of fuel and crashed",
        "That the radar system had been switched off for maintenance"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "She looked at him strangely and laughed, saying: 'Another aeroplane? Up there in this storm? No other aeroplanes were flying tonight. Yours was the only one I could see on the radar.'"
    },
    {
      q: "Why did Anne Frank decide to name her diary 'Kitty' and write to it as a personal friend?",
      opts: [
        "Because her school teacher instructed her to write fictitiously",
        "Because she believed that paper has more patience than people and lacked a true intimate confidant",
        "Because she was not allowed to speak to anyone in Amsterdam",
        "Because Kitty was her pet cat that had been left behind"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Anne famously remarked that 'paper has more patience than people' and wanted the diary to be the real, intimate friend she didn't have in daily life."
    },
    {
      q: "How did Anne Frank win over her mathematics teacher, Mr. Keesing, who was annoyed by her talking?",
      opts: [
        "By scoring the highest marks in all mathematics tests",
        "By writing a witty poem about a swan father biting his ducklings for quacking too much",
        "By maintaining complete silence for three whole months",
        "By having her father visit the school to plead her case"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Her third essay in verse portrayed a father swan who killed his ducklings because they quacked too much. Mr. Keesing appreciated the brilliant joke and never punished her for talking again."
